A settling chamber is used for the removal of discrete particulate matter from air with following conditions.
Horizontal velocity of air = 0.2 m/s;
Temperature of air stream = 77\(^\circ\)C;
Specific gravity of particle to be removed = 2.65;
Chamber length = 12 m;
Chamber height = 2 m;
Viscosity of air at 77\(^\circ\)C = 2.1 x 10\(^{-5}\) kg/m.s;
Acceleration due to gravity (g) = 9.81 m/s\(^2\);
Density of air at 77\(^\circ\)C = 1.0 kg/m\(^3\);
Assume the density of water as 1000 kg/m\(^3\) and Laminar condition exists in the chamber.
The minimum size of particle that will be removed with 100% efficiency in the settling chamber (in μm) is ______ (round off to one decimal place).
